---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Read Your Quilt Cutting Plan"
  description="Follow stock-bin allocations, purchased-fabric instructions, diagrams, and text alternatives from one selected geometry."
  eyebrow="Learn QuiltClarity · Cutting"
  guideSlug="read-your-cutting-plan"
  guideCategory="start_here"
  previous={{
    href: '/guides/read-your-shopping-plan/',
    label: 'Read Your Shopping Plan',
  }}
  next={{
    href: '/guides/print-your-project-plan/',
    label: 'Print Your Project Plan',
  }}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Cut from named stock first</h2><p>
      Existing-stock allocations are grouped by physical piece. Match each
      heading to the measured remnant or preset instance before cutting.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Then use the purchased-fabric plan</h2><p>
      The purchased section contains only requirements not allocated to stock.
      Raw bolt length explains the geometry; Buy now includes safety and
      purchase rounding.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Instructions and diagram agree</h2><p>
      Both are projected from the same placements. Use strip instructions where
      the geometry supports them. For irregular placements, follow the exact
      piece list and visual layout rather than inventing a simpler sequence.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use zoom and the text version</h2><p>
      Zoom changes only the on-screen view. Every diagram includes a complete
      text allocation with dimensions, piece groups, positions, and unused row
      width. The practical layout is deterministic but is not claimed as a
      proven global optimum.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
